From 3ad417f738cd82951d6636547cbc942ea64ab5f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:38:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] commands: run commands by the shell, pass arguments safely

The command line was split into words and every word with characters
other than [A-Za-z0-9_./|-] was quoted again. Because of this:

- pipes worked, but redirections, ";", "&&", variables, globs and
  scripts of several lines did not: "echo $HOME" printed "$HOME";
- an argument typed by the user went to the shell unquoted when it held
  only such characters, so "|reboot" ran reboot. For a command with
  "Public access" and "Custom arguments" anyone could run anything
  without logging in;
- "\ " and "\"" kept their backslash, unlike the shell;
- the public download link passed its arguments as an array and lost
  them; a command reading stdin waited on the HTTP request body.

Now the configured command is a piece of shell script run by /bin/sh -c,
as in a terminal. The arguments never reach the shell parser: they are
the positional parameters $1, $2, ... (set -- 'quoted' ...), and a
one-line command that does not use $1...$9 or "$@" itself gets "$@" at
its end, as before. After ";", "|", "&&", "then" or "do" nothing is
appended, so the arguments cannot become a command of their own. The
arguments are split by the shell rules for quotes and backslashes and
are never expanded: $(...), `...`, $HOME and * stay as typed. stdin is
/dev/null.

The helpers move to ucode/commands.uc (luci.commands), shared with the
rpcd plugin of the next patch. ESC of color codes no longer marks the
output as binary data. The public result page wraps long lines.

Checked: the argument parser against dash on 21 strings (quotes,
backslashes, Cyrillic, empty arguments); 78 checks of the parser,
positional detection, script building and binary test in node with the
ucode builtins; the built scripts run by dash keep "$(reboot)", "|",
";reboot" and "`id`" as plain text.

